  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Hygiene and Sanitation in the Catholic Diocese of Yei, South Sudan.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2013, Caritas Australia funded the construction of 70 community low cost pit latrines in Mundri East County, in the villages of Kediba, Wirlo and Wittos, serving 506 vulnerable beneficiaries. This has proven successful and has combated open defecation; thus reducing instances of water borne diseases. Following on from the successes of this project, and utilising the best practise gained from lessons learnt during the project implementation, the planned intervention aims to construct 100 community low cost pit latrines benefiting 100 households (700 individuals) in three locations in Mundri East county; Larugura, Mollo and Lakamadi. The result achieved by this action should be increased latrine coverage in the target area, a reduction in open defecation and reduction in cases of water bourn and communicable diseases.</narrative>
  </description>
